Hi David,

Of the 36 learners enrolled at the September close, 34 submitted a valid read=
ing memo and 27 scored at least 14 out of 20. That is 94.4% and 75.0% respect=
ively, both using the 36 enrolled learners as the denominator.

The attached report sets out the assessment and what we can reasonably conclu=
de from this task. The separate count sheet gives the score bands for the 34 =
marked submissions: seven below 14, 15 at 14=E2=80=9316 and 12 at 17=E2=80=93=
20. It contains aggregate counts rather than learner IDs.

The two learners without a valid submission have no scored value in their res=
ults; they are not included in the seven below 14. Kathleen and I have prepar=
ed an opportunity next term and plan to contact them individually about the p=
aper and optional consultation routes. The follow-up has not yet taken place.

Erin and I agreed the 8 / 6 / 6 criteria and used them to reread the remainin=
g valid submissions after moderation. I would welcome a chance to go through =
the report and the distinction between the ordinary advice and the question a=
bout unconfirmed approval with you this afternoon.

Thanks,
Heather

